From: apothecary <evororentals@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] HID: magicmouse: MTP positions are hundredths of a millimetre

The MTP trackpads report touch positions in 0.01 mm: macOS's multitouch
stack turns them into millimetres by dividing by 100. The resolution was
instead taken as the reported span over the surface's width and height
from the sensor dimensions report, which are the whole surface, wider
than the span touches are reported in. On the J414s that gives 98 units
per mm across and 97 up, 1.4 % and 2 % short, so every distance libinput
derives (tap and drag thresholds, palm and edge zones) is that far off,
and its scaling of y to x's resolution (98/97) makes vertical motion 1 %
faster than horizontal, which the hardware does not do. Report 100 on
both axes.

Not yet tested on hardware.

diff --git a/drivers/hid/hid-magicmouse.c b/drivers/hid/hid-magicmouse.c
index 2dd3f828441..fda66ee4f32 100644
--- a/drivers/hid/hid-magicmouse.c
+++ b/drivers/hid/hid-magicmouse.c
@@ -368,7 +368,6 @@ static int magicmouse_open(struct input_dev *dev)
 			__le16 max_x;
 			__le16 max_y;
 		} dim;
-		uint32_t x_span, y_span;
 
 		ret = hid_hw_raw_request(hdev, SENSOR_DIMENSIONS_REPORT_ID, buf, sizeof(buf), HID_FEATURE_REPORT, HID_REQ_GET_REPORT);
 		if (ret < (int)(1 + sizeof(dim))) {
@@ -384,12 +383,17 @@ static int magicmouse_open(struct input_dev *dev)
 		/* Y axis is inverted */
 		input_set_abs_params(input, ABS_MT_POSITION_Y,
 				     -le16_to_int(dim.max_y), -le16_to_int(dim.min_y), 0, 0);
-		x_span = le16_to_int(dim.max_x) - le16_to_int(dim.min_x);
-		y_span = le16_to_int(dim.max_y) - le16_to_int(dim.min_y);
-
-		/* X/Y resolution */
-		input_abs_set_res(input, ABS_MT_POSITION_X, 100 * x_span / le32_to_cpu(dim.width) );
-		input_abs_set_res(input, ABS_MT_POSITION_Y, 100 * y_span / le32_to_cpu(dim.height) );
+		/*
+		 * X/Y resolution. Positions are in hundredths of a millimetre:
+		 * macOS's multitouch stack divides them by 100 for millimetres.
+		 * The report's width and height are the whole surface, wider
+		 * than the span the sensor reports touches in, so dividing the
+		 * span by them under-states the resolution (98 and 97 on the
+		 * J414s), and libinput then scales y by a ratio the hardware
+		 * does not have.
+		 */
+		input_abs_set_res(input, ABS_MT_POSITION_X, 100);
+		input_abs_set_res(input, ABS_MT_POSITION_Y, 100);
 
 		/* copy info, as input_mt_init_slots() does */
 		dev->absinfo[ABS_X] = dev->absinfo[ABS_MT_POSITION_X];
